    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2610.36729v1</id>
    <title>Hy-Nomas: Towards Free-form Interactive World Generation</title>
    <updated>2026-10-27T06:48:59Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.36729v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2610.36729v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Interactive world generation requires models to follow successive commands while preserving relevant history and action consequences. We present Hy-Nomas, a video world model with an 8B diffusion backbone that supports free-form text instructions and continuous camera control across multiple interaction turns. It generates variable-length segments conditioned on current inputs and cached history. Our central design aligns structured video captions with action-aware causal attention: descriptive context remains accessible across segments, while action instructions are restricted to their intended temporal windows. A vision-language Prompt Enhancer (PE) translates user requests and multimodal interaction histories into structured conditions for the next segment. A multi-stage curriculum progressively introduces causal generation, text interaction, camera control, and training on model-generated histories, followed by diffusion distillation. In human evaluation, Hy-Nomas shows superior performance over existing world models. We release model weights, code and benchmarks, together with a lightweight adaptation workflow, to support reproducible research on interactive world generation.</summary>
